{#
  THE ONE FRONT DOOR, FROM A ROLE'S OWN SIGN-IN PAGE (owner, 29 Oct 2026; Account\Roles).

  The staff, judging and organisation sign-in pages keep working, and point to the Africa GATES
  account, which opens all of them. The direction matters: the PUBLIC sign-in still links to
  none of these pages (a shared public door is what makes a console a target); these pages
  link out to it. A member already signed in here who holds this role is offered a POST to
  switch — never a link, because switching starts a session.

  Takes: door_kind (admin|judge|org), door_next (where the role lands), door_p, door_btn (classes).
#}
{% set _acct = account_switch() %}
{% set _mine = _acct ? (_acct|filter(m => m.kind == door_kind and m.live)|length > 0) : false %}
{% if _mine %}
  <form method="post" action="/account/switch">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}"><input type="hidden" name="kind" value="{{ door_kind }}">
    <button class="{{ door_btn }}" type="submit">{{ 'Continue with your Africa GATES account'|trans }}</button>
  </form>
{% else %}
  <p class="{{ door_p }}">{{ 'Have an Africa GATES account?'|trans }} <a href="/account/login?next={{ door_next|url_encode }}">{{ 'Sign in with it'|trans }}</a>{{ ' — a sign-in under the same email is added to it once, then one sign-in opens both.'|trans }}</p>
{% endif %}
